Package: tee-cell-stream-server
Version: @VERSION@
Section: net
Priority: optional
Architecture: amd64
Maintainer: TEE <github@teebug.de>
Installed-Size: @INSTALLED_SIZE@
Depends: python3 (>= 3.12), python3-gi, gir1.2-gtk-4.0, gir1.2-adw-1, gir1.2-glib-2.0, python3-evdev, ffmpeg, libc6 (>= 2.38), libva2, libva-drm2, libdrm2, libxcb1, libxcb-shm0, libxcb-shape0, libxcb-xfixes0, libpulse0, zlib1g, gstreamer1.0-tools, gstreamer1.0-pipewire, gstreamer1.0-plugins-base, gstreamer1.0-plugins-good, xdg-desktop-portal, iproute2, xdg-utils, udev, libxkbcommon0
Recommends: xdg-desktop-portal-gnome | xdg-desktop-portal-gtk, gnome-shell-extension-appindicator, x11-xserver-utils
Homepage: https://github.com/TheErsysEnding/TEE-PS3-Remoteplay-PC-games-on-PS3-Streaming
Description: TEE Cell Stream Server - stream the PC desktop to a PS3 (cell-stream)
 Linux port of cell-stream-server: captures the desktop (xdg-desktop-portal /
 PipeWire, X11 fallback), encodes H.264 on the GPU (NVENC, VA-API, AMF) or CPU
 (x264), streams it over UDP to a PS3 running the cell-stream homebrew app
 (720p60, ~25 ms), sends the PC's sound along, and turns the PS3 controller
 into a virtual Xbox 360 gamepad or into mouse and keyboard on the PC.
 .
 Brings its own ffmpeg 8.0.1 with two patches (NVENC without the deblocking
 filter and on whole pixels, MPEG-2 intra refresh) and falls back to the
 distribution's ffmpeg when it cannot run.
 .
 Modern GTK4/libadwaita window with tray icon; the PS3 finds the server on
 its own (discovery beacon). Wire protocol identical to the Windows original
 (ps3-dev release 174-a5dd795, Apache-2.0).
 .
 Needs a PS3 running HEN or CFW with the cell-stream homebrew installed - this
 package is only the PC half. The interface is in English and German; the
 bundled guide (/usr/share/doc/tee-cell-stream-server/ANLEITUNG.md) is German.
